{:receipt :nbb/tier-audit
 :date "2026-08-17"
 :question
 "kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer advertised nbb as a third test platform alongside
  the JVM and self-hosted cljs. It had been dead: `npm run test:nbb` failed in
  the ANALYSIS phase on `cljs.core.ExceptionInfo`, so 0 of 17 namespaces ran,
  while the JVM and cljs tiers stayed green and nobody was told. Fixed in
  b8032efa941. Nobody had checked whether any other repository had the same
  problem. This is that check."

 :why-it-matters
 "The workspace runtime order (superproject CLAUDE.md) is
  `kotoba wasm > clojurewasm > ClojureScript > nbb`, with the JVM and bb
  explicitly demoted to last resort. A dead nbb tier means the tier the
  workspace prefers is not being exercised while the one it deprecates is."

