 ;; ------------------------------------------------------------------ method
 :method
 {:how-each-tier-was-run
  "The pinned tree was extracted with `git archive <pin> | tar -x` into a fresh
   scratchpad directory (or, for pins absent locally, the GitHub tarball at that
   sha). `npm install` where package.json declares dependencies. Then the exact
   command string from package.json / gates.edn, through /bin/sh."
  :never "No test was run inside orgs/. Verified afterwards: the shared checkouts
          and the superproject's package.json / package-lock.json / node_modules
          are unmodified."

  :harness-defects-found-and-fixed-mid-audit
  ["A first pass symlinked whole org trees into the work directory so that
    ../sibling classpaths would resolve. That made it possible for a later
    candidate to be run through a symlink INTO the shared west checkout. Caught
    by reading a stack trace whose path began /Users/junkawasaki/github/. No
    damage occurred (checked: clean), and materialize now lstats and unlinks a
    symlink before extracting."
   "Two of thirteen shard processes CRASHED partway through on
    `Cannot read properties of null (reading 'trim')` -- my own error-summarising
    function called str/trim on the last line of empty output. The partial
    results looked exactly like complete ones. Every candidate from those shards
    was re-run after the fix; the merge takes the later run."
   "Three results that the batch reported as failures were the harness's fault,
    not the repo's, and were only separated by re-running each one individually
    in clean isolation: network-awai/loop-yakuwari (sibling not materialized --
    actually 46 tests green), gftdcojp/misogi and network-awai/local-murakumo
    (same). Had I reported the batch numbers I would have named three healthy
    repos as broken."
   "My own summarising script died on `Unable to resolve symbol: format` -- the
    same class of nbb analysis-phase failure this audit is about, in the audit's
    own tooling."]

  :every-non-green-result-was-re-verified-individually
  "16 did-not-run + 3 red were each re-materialized alone and re-run by hand. 9
   survived as real defects; 7 turned out to need setup; 3 red were confirmed as
   running. The batch number alone would have been wrong in both directions."

  :every-fix-was-measured-both-ways
  "For each of the six fixes: the advertised command was run first and observed
   to produce 0 tests, then the fixed command was run and observed to produce a
   specific test count. No fix was landed on the argument that it looked right."}

